From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: conda developers <conda@conda.io>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mark libmambapy bindings module as GIL-not-used for
 freethreaded Python 3.14t support

Declares the pybind11 module with pybind11::mod_gil_not_used() so that
the module can be imported in a freethreaded (cp314t) Python interpreter
without triggering the GIL-required import guard introduced in
pybind11 >= 2.13.

bindings.hpp only exposes the full pybind11:: namespace (no `py` alias),
so the full namespace qualifier is used here rather than py::mod_gil_not_used().

See: https://pybind11.readthedocs.io/en/stable/advanced/misc.html#freethreading
---
 libmambapy/bindings/bindings.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libmambapy/bindings/bindings.cpp b/libmambapy/bindings/bindings.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/libmambapy/bindings/bindings.cpp
+++ b/libmambapy/bindings/bindings.cpp
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 #include "bindings.hpp"

-PYBIND11_MODULE(bindings, m)
+PYBIND11_MODULE(bindings, m, pybind11::mod_gil_not_used())
 {
     mambapy::bind_submodule_utils(m.def_submodule("utils"));
     mambapy::bind_submodule_specs(m.def_submodule("specs"));
